WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.260
In a February Gallup poll, 72% of
Americans viewed Russia unfavorably. This

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.639
is the highest negative rating in three
decades. Americans clearly believe that

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:19.650
Russia tried to interfere in the 2016 US
election. In January and March Quinnipiac

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.580
University surveys, around 70% of
registered voters said that it did.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.320
People want the Russia investigation to
continue, and most people feel confident

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.790
that Special Counsel Robert Muller will
conduct a fair investigation. In three

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.690
identically worded questions asked by
Pew from November through early March,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:42.809
between 55% and 61% felt confident.
Looking forward, Americans are concerned

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:48.329
about the November 2018 elections. In a
new Marist Poll, 51% said

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.320
that it was likely that there would be
Russian interference in them. 41%

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.910
said it was not very or not likely at
all. And they want President Trump to do

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:02.250
more. In the March Quinnipiac University
poll, 61% of registered voters said that

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.020
the Trump administration should be doing
more to protect the elections from Russian interference.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.860
What do you think
about the Russia investigation? Let us

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.640
know in your comments. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.930
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.520
research and videos from AEI.

